to retire from the court, paving the way for

00:01:03.539 --> 00:01:04.799
a Biden appointment.

00:01:04.799 --> 00:01:11.200
The liberal justices decision to step down
after more than 27 years on the court allows

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:16.119
Biden to appoint a successor who could serve
four decades.

00:01:16.119 --> 00:01:21.640
Biden and Breyer are scheduled to appear together
at the White House today as the Supreme Court

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.259
will announce his retirement.

00:01:23.259 --> 00:01:25.930
That may have happened by the time you listen
to today's show.

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:31.710
Brian is one of three Breyer or rather is
one of the three remaining liberal justices.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:36.689
His decision to retire after more than 27
years on the court allows Biden to appoint

00:01:36.689 --> 00:01:42.179
a successor who could serve for decades in
the short term, maintaining the current six

00:01:42.179 --> 00:01:46.710
